(701,654,$mw$9D183ED8547A992AD3A7840CD15F1411821080C582F0CFD03CC5E697228857B3$mw$,$mw$981e5ca61fe0ca0603d4b6af52651874$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":654,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تحديد نهاية متتالية هندسية متناقصة","TitleEn":"Find the limit of a decreasing geometric sequence","QuestionTextAr":"لـ n ≥ 1، اعتبر aₙ = (1/2)ⁿ. ما نهايتها؟","QuestionTextEn":"For n ≥ 1 let aₙ = (1/2)ⁿ. What is its limit?","DetailedSolutionAr":"بما أن النسبة 1/2 بين صفر وواحد، فإن حدود المتتالية موجبة ومتناقصة وتقترب من صفر.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Because the ratio 1/2 is between 0 and 1, terms stay positive, decrease, and tend to zero.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2605,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2606,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2607,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2608,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\infty","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"افحص القيمة المطلقة للأساس.","En":"Check the absolute ratio."},{"Ar":"طبق نهاية المتتالية الهندسية.","En":"Apply the geometric sequence limit."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تحديد نهاية متتالية هندسية متناقصة","En":"Find the limit of a decreasing geometric sequence"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"النسبة 1/2 عامل الانتقال لا النهاية.","En":"1/2 is the common ratio, not the limit."}},{"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 هو الحد عند n=0، وليس النهاية.","En":"1 is the term at n=0, not the limit."}},{"LatexCode":"\\infty","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المتتالية متناقصة ومحصورة بين صفر ونصف، فلا تتباعد إلى اللانهاية.","En":"The sequence decreases and is bounded between zero and one half, so it cannot diverge to infinity."}}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"لـ n ≥ 1، اعتبر aₙ = (1/2)ⁿ. ما نهايتها؟","En":"For n ≥ 1 let aₙ = (1/2)ⁿ. What is its limit?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"المتتالية الهندسية ذات الأساس نصف تؤول إلى الصفر.","En":"A geometric sequence of ratio one half tends to zero."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"كل حد يساوي نصف سابقه، وتبقى الحدود موجبة.","En":"Each term is half its predecessor and all terms remain positive."},{"Ar":"المتتالية متناقصة ومحدودة من أسفل بالصفر، إذن لها نهاية L.","En":"The sequence decreases and is bounded below by zero, so it has a limit L."},{"Ar":"بتمرير النهاية في العلاقة نحصل على $L=L/2$، ومن ثم $L=0$.","En":"Passing to the limit in the recurrence gives $L=L/2$, hence $L=0$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$0$","En":"$0$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط أساس المتتالية مع نهايتها.","En":"Do not confuse the common ratio with the limit."},"FormulaLatex":"a_{n+1}=\\frac12a_n\\Rightarrow L=\\frac12L","Substitution":{"Ar":"$L=0$","En":"$L=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$0< (1/2)^n\\le 1/2$","En":"$0< (1/2)^n\\le 1/2$"}},"TrackIds":[13,20],"CategoryId":36,"PrimarySkillId":74,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"افحص القيمة المطلقة للأساس.","En":"Check the absolute ratio."},{"Ar":"طبق نهاية المتتالية الهندسية.","En":"Apply the geometric sequence limit."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"المتتالية الهندسية ذات الأساس نصف تؤول إلى الصفر.","En":"A geometric sequence of ratio one half tends to zero."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"كل حد يساوي نصف سابقه، وتبقى الحدود موجبة.","En":"Each term is half its predecessor and all terms remain positive."},{"Ar":"المتتالية متناقصة ومحدودة من أسفل بالصفر، إذن لها نهاية L.","En":"The sequence decreases and is bounded below by zero, so it has a limit L."},{"Ar":"بتمرير النهاية في العلاقة نحصل على $L=L/2$، ومن ثم $L=0$.","En":"Passing to the limit in the recurrence gives $L=L/2$, hence $L=0$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$0$","En":"$0$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط أساس المتتالية مع نهايتها.","En":"Do not confuse the common ratio with the limit."},"FormulaLatex":"a_{n+1}=\\frac12a_n\\Rightarrow L=\\frac12L","Substitution":{"Ar":"$L=0$","En":"$L=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$0< (1/2)^n\\le 1/2$","En":"$0< (1/2)^n\\le 1/2$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"النسبة 1/2 عامل الانتقال لا النهاية.","En":"1/2 is the common ratio, not the limit."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 هو الحد عند n=0، وليس النهاية.","En":"1 is the term at n=0, not the limit."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المتتالية متناقصة ومحصورة بين صفر ونصف، فلا تتباعد إلى اللانهاية.","En":"The sequence decreases and is bounded between zero and one half, so it cannot diverge to infinity."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$المتتالية الهندسية ذات الأساس نصف تؤول إلى الصفر.

$a_{n+1}=\frac12a_n\Rightarrow L=\frac12L$

1. كل حد يساوي نصف سابقه، وتبقى الحدود موجبة.

2. المتتالية متناقصة ومحدودة من أسفل بالصفر، إذن لها نهاية L.

3. بتمرير النهاية في العلاقة نحصل على $L=L/2$، ومن ثم $L=0$.

$L=0$

$0$ بلا وحدة قياس

$0< (1/2)^n\le 1/2$

لا تخلط أساس المتتالية مع نهايتها.$mw$,$mw$A geometric sequence of ratio one half tends to zero.

$a_{n+1}=\frac12a_n\Rightarrow L=\frac12L$

1. Each term is half its predecessor and all terms remain positive.

2. The sequence decreases and is bounded below by zero, so it has a limit L.

3. Passing to the limit in the recurrence gives $L=L/2$, hence $L=0$.

$L=0$

$0$ Dimensionless

$0< (1/2)^n\le 1/2$

Do not confuse the common ratio with the limit.$mw$),
(702,655,$mw$9131852EA00FF8505E40CA2357E1E395F0A34A0CBA8F885EEC87F8B2E2C74202$mw$,$mw$1cd4c6ee33038287df80f3779d292e2d$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":655,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تفسير تقارب مجاميع جزئية متزايدة ومحدودة","TitleEn":"Determine a limit of increasing bounded partial sums","QuestionTextAr":"لتكن aₙ = 1/2 + 1/4 + ⋯ + 1/2ⁿ. ما نهاية aₙ عند n → ∞؟","QuestionTextEn":"Let aₙ = 1/2 + 1/4 + ⋯ + 1/2ⁿ. What is lim aₙ as n → ∞?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المجموع الجزئي لمتسلسلة هندسية = 1 − (1/2)ⁿ. وهو متزايد وأصغر من 1 ونهايته 1.","DetailedSolutionEn":"The partial geometric sum is 1 − (1/2)ⁿ. It increases, stays below 1 and tends to 1.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2609,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2610,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2611,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2612,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\infty","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"اعتبر التعبير مجموعاً هندسياً جزئياً.","En":"Treat the expression as a finite geometric sum."},{"Ar":"اكتب صيغة المجموع الجزئي ثم خذ النهاية عندما يزداد عدد الحدود بلا حد.","En":"Write the partial sum formula, then take its limit as the number of terms grows."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تفسير تقارب مجاميع جزئية متزايدة ومحدودة","En":"Determine a limit of increasing bounded partial sums"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"هذا الحد الأول وحده وليس مجموع الحدود.","En":"This is just the first term, not the sum."}},{"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2 مجموع المتسلسلة التي تبدأ من 1 لا من نصف.","En":"Two is the sum of the series starting at one rather than one half."}},{"LatexCode":"\\infty","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المجموع الجزئي أصغر من واحد فلا يتجه إلى اللانهاية.","En":"The partial sum stays below one and cannot tend to infinity."}}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"لتكن aₙ = 1/2 + 1/4 + ⋯ + 1/2ⁿ. ما نهاية aₙ عند n → ∞؟","En":"Let aₙ = 1/2 + 1/4 + ⋯ + 1/2ⁿ. What is lim aₙ as n → ∞?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون المجموع الهندسي المنتهي: $S_n=a(1-r^n)/(1-r)$ عندما $r\\ne1$، وهنا $a=r=1/2$.","En":"Finite geometric sum: $S_n=a(1-r^n)/(1-r)$ for $r\\ne1$, with $a=r=1/2$."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نحدد الحد الأول والنسبة: كلاهما 1/2.","En":"The first term and ratio are both 1/2."},{"Ar":"نعوض في مجموع n حدود فنحصل على $a_n=1-(1/2)^n$.","En":"Substitute into the finite sum to obtain $a_n=1-(1/2)^n$."},{"Ar":"بما أن القيمة المطلقة للنسبة أقل من واحد، يزول الحد الأسي في النهاية.","En":"Because the absolute ratio is below one, the exponential term vanishes in the limit."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$1$","En":"$1$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط نهاية مجموع الحدود بنهاية الحد المفرد.","En":"Do not confuse the limit of partial sums with the limit of individual terms."},"FormulaLatex":"S_n=\\frac{a_1(1-r^n)}{1-r},\\quad r\\ne1","Substitution":{"Ar":"$1-(1/2)^n\\to1$","En":"$1-(1/2)^n\\to1$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$1-a_n=(1/2)^n\\to0$","En":"$1-a_n=(1/2)^n\\to0$"}},"TrackIds":[13,20],"CategoryId":36,"PrimarySkillId":74,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"اعتبر التعبير مجموعاً هندسياً جزئياً.","En":"Treat the expression as a finite geometric sum."},{"Ar":"اكتب صيغة المجموع الجزئي ثم خذ النهاية عندما يزداد عدد الحدود بلا حد.","En":"Write the partial sum formula, then take its limit as the number of terms grows."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون المجموع الهندسي المنتهي: $S_n=a(1-r^n)/(1-r)$ عندما $r\\ne1$، وهنا $a=r=1/2$.","En":"Finite geometric sum: $S_n=a(1-r^n)/(1-r)$ for $r\\ne1$, with $a=r=1/2$."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نحدد الحد الأول والنسبة: كلاهما 1/2.","En":"The first term and ratio are both 1/2."},{"Ar":"نعوض في مجموع n حدود فنحصل على $a_n=1-(1/2)^n$.","En":"Substitute into the finite sum to obtain $a_n=1-(1/2)^n$."},{"Ar":"بما أن القيمة المطلقة للنسبة أقل من واحد، يزول الحد الأسي في النهاية.","En":"Because the absolute ratio is below one, the exponential term vanishes in the limit."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$1$","En":"$1$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط نهاية مجموع الحدود بنهاية الحد المفرد.","En":"Do not confuse the limit of partial sums with the limit of individual terms."},"FormulaLatex":"S_n=\\frac{a_1(1-r^n)}{1-r},\\quad r\\ne1","Substitution":{"Ar":"$1-(1/2)^n\\to1$","En":"$1-(1/2)^n\\to1$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$1-a_n=(1/2)^n\\to0$","En":"$1-a_n=(1/2)^n\\to0$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"هذا الحد الأول وحده وليس مجموع الحدود.","En":"This is just the first term, not the sum."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2 مجموع المتسلسلة التي تبدأ من 1 لا من نصف.","En":"Two is the sum of the series starting at one rather than one half."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المجموع الجزئي أصغر من واحد فلا يتجه إلى اللانهاية.","En":"The partial sum stays below one and cannot tend to infinity."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$قانون المجموع الهندسي المنتهي: $S_n=a(1-r^n)/(1-r)$ عندما $r\ne1$، وهنا $a=r=1/2$.

$S_n=\frac{a_1(1-r^n)}{1-r},\quad r\ne1$

1. نحدد الحد الأول والنسبة: كلاهما 1/2.

2. نعوض في مجموع n حدود فنحصل على $a_n=1-(1/2)^n$.

3. بما أن القيمة المطلقة للنسبة أقل من واحد، يزول الحد الأسي في النهاية.

$1-(1/2)^n\to1$

$1$ بلا وحدة قياس

$1-a_n=(1/2)^n\to0$

لا تخلط نهاية مجموع الحدود بنهاية الحد المفرد.$mw$,$mw$Finite geometric sum: $S_n=a(1-r^n)/(1-r)$ for $r\ne1$, with $a=r=1/2$.

$S_n=\frac{a_1(1-r^n)}{1-r},\quad r\ne1$

1. The first term and ratio are both 1/2.

2. Substitute into the finite sum to obtain $a_n=1-(1/2)^n$.

3. Because the absolute ratio is below one, the exponential term vanishes in the limit.

$1-(1/2)^n\to1$

$1$ Dimensionless

$1-a_n=(1/2)^n\to0$

Do not confuse the limit of partial sums with the limit of individual terms.$mw$),
(703,656,$mw$59FBADAEFF580D84F2FE0B168CE0B4CB27F3B8CE682BAE3E14DE755FC98278F1$mw$,$mw$a2298c93ba0d343c49001e88947195de$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":656,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"إثبات تقارب متتالية معرفة بعلاقة تراجعية","TitleEn":"Find a monotone recurrence's fixed-point limit","QuestionTextAr":"متتالية تبدأ بـ a₁ = 2، ثم aₙ₊₁ = (aₙ + 6)/2. إذا كانت متزايدة ومحدودة، فما نهايتها؟","QuestionTextEn":"A sequence starts at a₁ = 2 and satisfies aₙ₊₁ = (aₙ + 6)/2. Assuming it is increasing and bounded, what is its limit?","DetailedSolutionAr":"إذا كانت النهاية L، فبالمرور للنهاية: L = (L + 6)/2، إذن 2L = L + 6 ومنه L = 6. وفعلاً 2، 4، 5، 5.5… متزايدة ومحدودة بـ6.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Let the limit be L. Then L = (L + 6)/2, giving L = 6. The terms 2, 4, 5, 5.5, ... increase and remain below 6.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2613,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2614,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"4","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2615,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"6","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2616,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"استعمل فرضية التقارب المعطاة.","En":"Use the given convergence assumption."},{"Ar":"عوّض الحدين المتتاليين بنهايتهما المشتركة وحل المعادلة.","En":"Replace successive terms by their common limit and solve."}],"Title":{"Ar":"إثبات تقارب متتالية معرفة بعلاقة تراجعية","En":"Find a monotone recurrence's fixed-point limit"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2 قيمة البداية وليست نقطة ثابتة: (2+6)/2=4.","En":"Two is the initial term, not a fixed point: (2+6)/2=4."}},{"LatexCode":"4","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"4 هو الحد الثاني؛ (4+6)/2=5.","En":"Four is the second term; (4+6)/2=5."}},{"LatexCode":"6","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"12 ليس نقطة ثابتة لأن (12+6)/2=9.","En":"Twelve is not a fixed point since (12+6)/2=9."}}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"متتالية تبدأ بـ a₁ = 2، ثم aₙ₊₁ = (aₙ + 6)/2. إذا كانت متزايدة ومحدودة، فما نهايتها؟","En":"A sequence starts at a₁ = 2 and satisfies aₙ₊₁ = (aₙ + 6)/2. Assuming it is increasing and bounded, what is its limit?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الرتابة والانحصار يضمنان وجود النهاية، واستمرارية الطرف الأيمن تسمح بتمرير النهاية في التراجع.","En":"Monotonicity and boundedness ensure convergence; continuity permits passing the limit through the recurrence."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"فرض الرتابة والانحصار يضمن وجود نهاية حقيقية L.","En":"Monotonicity and boundedness guarantee a real limit L."},{"Ar":"الحد التالي له النهاية نفسها؛ والدالة (x+6)/2 مستمرة.","En":"The shifted sequence has the same limit, and (x+6)/2 is continuous."},{"Ar":"إذن $2L=L+6$، وبطرح L نحصل على $L=6$.","En":"Thus $2L=L+6$; subtract L to obtain $L=6$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$6$","En":"$6$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستنتج التقارب من معادلة النقطة الثابتة وحدها؛ استعمل الفرض المعطى.","En":"Do not infer convergence solely from a fixed-point equation; use the given assumption."},"FormulaLatex":"L=\\frac{L+6}{2}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$2L=L+6\\Rightarrow L=6$","En":"$2L=L+6\\Rightarrow L=6$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$6-a_n=4(1/2)^{n-1}\\to0$","En":"$6-a_n=4(1/2)^{n-1}\\to0$"}},"TrackIds":[13,20],"CategoryId":36,"PrimarySkillId":74,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"استعمل فرضية التقارب المعطاة.","En":"Use the given convergence assumption."},{"Ar":"عوّض الحدين المتتاليين بنهايتهما المشتركة وحل المعادلة.","En":"Replace successive terms by their common limit and solve."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الرتابة والانحصار يضمنان وجود النهاية، واستمرارية الطرف الأيمن تسمح بتمرير النهاية في التراجع.","En":"Monotonicity and boundedness ensure convergence; continuity permits passing the limit through the recurrence."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"فرض الرتابة والانحصار يضمن وجود نهاية حقيقية L.","En":"Monotonicity and boundedness guarantee a real limit L."},{"Ar":"الحد التالي له النهاية نفسها؛ والدالة (x+6)/2 مستمرة.","En":"The shifted sequence has the same limit, and (x+6)/2 is continuous."},{"Ar":"إذن $2L=L+6$، وبطرح L نحصل على $L=6$.","En":"Thus $2L=L+6$; subtract L to obtain $L=6$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$6$","En":"$6$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستنتج التقارب من معادلة النقطة الثابتة وحدها؛ استعمل الفرض المعطى.","En":"Do not infer convergence solely from a fixed-point equation; use the given assumption."},"FormulaLatex":"L=\\frac{L+6}{2}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$2L=L+6\\Rightarrow L=6$","En":"$2L=L+6\\Rightarrow L=6$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$6-a_n=4(1/2)^{n-1}\\to0$","En":"$6-a_n=4(1/2)^{n-1}\\to0$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2 قيمة البداية وليست نقطة ثابتة: (2+6)/2=4.","En":"Two is the initial term, not a fixed point: (2+6)/2=4."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"4 هو الحد الثاني؛ (4+6)/2=5.","En":"Four is the second term; (4+6)/2=5."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"12 ليس نقطة ثابتة لأن (12+6)/2=9.","En":"Twelve is not a fixed point since (12+6)/2=9."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الرتابة والانحصار يضمنان وجود النهاية، واستمرارية الطرف الأيمن تسمح بتمرير النهاية في التراجع.

$L=\frac{L+6}{2}$

1. فرض الرتابة والانحصار يضمن وجود نهاية حقيقية L.

2. الحد التالي له النهاية نفسها؛ والدالة (x+6)/2 مستمرة.

3. إذن $2L=L+6$، وبطرح L نحصل على $L=6$.

$2L=L+6\Rightarrow L=6$

$6$ بلا وحدة قياس

$6-a_n=4(1/2)^{n-1}\to0$

لا تستنتج التقارب من معادلة النقطة الثابتة وحدها؛ استعمل الفرض المعطى.$mw$,$mw$Monotonicity and boundedness ensure convergence; continuity permits passing the limit through the recurrence.

$L=\frac{L+6}{2}$

1. Monotonicity and boundedness guarantee a real limit L.

2. The shifted sequence has the same limit, and (x+6)/2 is continuous.

3. Thus $2L=L+6$; subtract L to obtain $L=6$.

$2L=L+6\Rightarrow L=6$

$6$ Dimensionless

$6-a_n=4(1/2)^{n-1}\to0$

Do not infer convergence solely from a fixed-point equation; use the given assumption.$mw$),
(704,689,$mw$14DCAAA3E81489227B8688579B8A70BB13F691252EB1E89E2036E7C92EA12318$mw$,$mw$38c4ad34a6e0a040ee101cd6b8ffdfae$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":689,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":2,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"فهم مجهول في مجموعات متساوية","TitleEn":"Find the unit quantity in equal groups","QuestionTextAr":"وُزّعت 54 كرة بالتساوي على 6 صناديق. إذا كان في كل صندوق x كرة، فما قيمة x؟","QuestionTextEn":"54 balls are distributed equally across 6 boxes. If each box holds x balls, what is x?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: في التوزيع بالتساوي يكون نصيب كل صندوق = العدد الكلي ÷ عدد الصناديق. لدينا 54 كرة وستة صناديق؛ نكتب 6س = 54 ثم نقسم على 6 لنحصل على س = 54 ÷ 6 = 9 كرات لكل صندوق. التحقق: 6 × 9 = 54.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Equal sharing means the amount per box equals the total divided by the number of boxes. For 54 balls in 6 boxes, 6x = 54, so x = 54 ÷ 6 = 9 balls per box. Check: 6 × 9 = 54.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2809,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"6","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2810,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"8","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2811,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"9","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2812,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في مجموعات متساوية أو في عكس الضرب.","En":"Think of equal groups or inverse multiplication."},{"Ar":"اقسم العدد الكلي على المعامل غير الصفري.","En":"Divide the total by the nonzero coefficient."}],"Title":{"Ar":"فهم مجهول في مجموعات متساوية","En":"Find the unit quantity in equal groups"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"6","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"6 كرات في الصندوق تعطي 36 فقط.","En":"Six per box totals only 36."}},{"LatexCode":"8","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"8 تعطي 48 كرة.","En":"Eight per box totals 48."}},{"LatexCode":"9","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"12 تعطي 72 كرة.","En":"Twelve per box totals 72."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"وُزّعت 54 كرة بالتساوي على 6 صناديق. إذا كان في كل صندوق x كرة، فما قيمة x؟","En":"54 balls are distributed equally across 6 boxes. If each box holds x balls, what is x?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نقسم الكمية الكلية على عدد المجموعات المتساوية، أو نقسم طرفي المعادلة على المعامل.","En":"Divide the total by the number of equal groups, or divide both sides by the coefficient."},"Unit":{"Ar":"كرة لكل صندوق","En":"balls per box"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نكتب عدد الكرات في ستة صناديق متساوية على صورة 6x.","En":"Six equal boxes contain 6x balls."},{"Ar":"نقسم 54 على 6 لأن كل صندوق له الحصة نفسها.","En":"Divide 54 by six because the boxes have equal shares."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$9$","En":"$9$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط عدد الصناديق بعدد الكرات في الصندوق الواحد.","En":"Do not confuse the number of boxes with balls per box."},"FormulaLatex":"6x=54\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{54}{6}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=9$","En":"$x=9$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$6\\times9=54$","En":"$6\\times9=54$"}},"TrackIds":[3],"CategoryId":2,"PrimarySkillId":9,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في مجموعات متساوية أو في عكس الضرب.","En":"Think of equal groups or inverse multiplication."},{"Ar":"اقسم العدد الكلي على المعامل غير الصفري.","En":"Divide the total by the nonzero coefficient."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نقسم الكمية الكلية على عدد المجموعات المتساوية، أو نقسم طرفي المعادلة على المعامل.","En":"Divide the total by the number of equal groups, or divide both sides by the coefficient."},"Unit":{"Ar":"كرة لكل صندوق","En":"balls per box"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نكتب عدد الكرات في ستة صناديق متساوية على صورة 6x.","En":"Six equal boxes contain 6x balls."},{"Ar":"نقسم 54 على 6 لأن كل صندوق له الحصة نفسها.","En":"Divide 54 by six because the boxes have equal shares."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$9$","En":"$9$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط عدد الصناديق بعدد الكرات في الصندوق الواحد.","En":"Do not confuse the number of boxes with balls per box."},"FormulaLatex":"6x=54\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{54}{6}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=9$","En":"$x=9$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$6\\times9=54$","En":"$6\\times9=54$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"6 كرات في الصندوق تعطي 36 فقط.","En":"Six per box totals only 36."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"8 تعطي 48 كرة.","En":"Eight per box totals 48."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"12 تعطي 72 كرة.","En":"Twelve per box totals 72."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نقسم الكمية الكلية على عدد المجموعات المتساوية، أو نقسم طرفي المعادلة على المعامل.

$6x=54\Rightarrow x=\frac{54}{6}$

1. نكتب عدد الكرات في ستة صناديق متساوية على صورة 6x.

2. نقسم 54 على 6 لأن كل صندوق له الحصة نفسها.

$x=9$

$9$ كرة لكل صندوق

$6\times9=54$

لا تخلط عدد الصناديق بعدد الكرات في الصندوق الواحد.$mw$,$mw$Divide the total by the number of equal groups, or divide both sides by the coefficient.

$6x=54\Rightarrow x=\frac{54}{6}$

1. Six equal boxes contain 6x balls.

2. Divide 54 by six because the boxes have equal shares.

$x=9$

$9$ balls per box

$6\times9=54$

Do not confuse the number of boxes with balls per box.$mw$),
(705,690,$mw$6A69A36A955C25F62A00675603DA673A406217B728C713227DE195BC465C2AF2$mw$,$mw$24336c2104683fb9a347e1e2fc26cca6$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":690,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":2,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"حل معادلة أحادية الخطوة بالضرب","TitleEn":"Solve a one-step multiplication equation","QuestionTextAr":"أي قيمة للمتغير k تحقق 7k = 91؟","QuestionTextEn":"Which value of k satisfies 7k = 91?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: نقسم طرفي المعادلة على معامل المتغير لعزله. من 7k = 91 نحصل على k = 91 ÷ 7 = 13. التحقق بالتعويض: 7 × 13 = 91، لذلك قيمة k الصحيحة هي 13.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Isolate a variable by dividing both sides by its coefficient. From 7k = 91, calculate k = 91 ÷ 7 = 13. Check: 7 × 13 = 91, confirming k = 13.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2813,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"11","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2814,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2815,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"13","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2816,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"14","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في مجموعات متساوية أو في عكس الضرب.","En":"Think of equal groups or inverse multiplication."},{"Ar":"اقسم العدد الكلي على المعامل غير الصفري.","En":"Divide the total by the nonzero coefficient."}],"Title":{"Ar":"حل معادلة أحادية الخطوة بالضرب","En":"Solve a one-step multiplication equation"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"11","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"7×11=77 وليس 91.","En":"7×11=77, not 91."}},{"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"7×12=84 وليس 91.","En":"7×12=84, not 91."}},{"LatexCode":"13","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"14","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"7×14=98 وليس 91.","En":"7×14=98, not 91."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"أي قيمة للمتغير k تحقق 7k = 91؟","En":"Which value of k satisfies 7k = 91?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نقسم الكمية الكلية على عدد المجموعات المتساوية، أو نقسم طرفي المعادلة على المعامل.","En":"Divide the total by the number of equal groups, or divide both sides by the coefficient."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المعامل 7 غير صفري، لذا نقسم الطرفين عليه.","En":"The coefficient seven is nonzero, so divide both sides by it."},{"Ar":"نحسب خارج قسمة 91 على 7 فنحصل على 13.","En":"Compute 91 divided by seven to get 13."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$13$","En":"$13$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تطرح المعامل بدلاً من القسمة عليه.","En":"Do not subtract the coefficient instead of dividing by it."},"FormulaLatex":"7k=91\\Rightarrow k=\\frac{91}{7}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$k=13$","En":"$k=13$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$7(13)=91$","En":"$7(13)=91$"}},"TrackIds":[4],"CategoryId":2,"PrimarySkillId":9,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في مجموعات متساوية أو في عكس الضرب.","En":"Think of equal groups or inverse multiplication."},{"Ar":"اقسم العدد الكلي على المعامل غير الصفري.","En":"Divide the total by the nonzero coefficient."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نقسم الكمية الكلية على عدد المجموعات المتساوية، أو نقسم طرفي المعادلة على المعامل.","En":"Divide the total by the number of equal groups, or divide both sides by the coefficient."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المعامل 7 غير صفري، لذا نقسم الطرفين عليه.","En":"The coefficient seven is nonzero, so divide both sides by it."},{"Ar":"نحسب خارج قسمة 91 على 7 فنحصل على 13.","En":"Compute 91 divided by seven to get 13."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$13$","En":"$13$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تطرح المعامل بدلاً من القسمة عليه.","En":"Do not subtract the coefficient instead of dividing by it."},"FormulaLatex":"7k=91\\Rightarrow k=\\frac{91}{7}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$k=13$","En":"$k=13$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$7(13)=91$","En":"$7(13)=91$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"7×11=77 وليس 91.","En":"7×11=77, not 91."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"7×12=84 وليس 91.","En":"7×12=84, not 91."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"7×14=98 وليس 91.","En":"7×14=98, not 91."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نقسم الكمية الكلية على عدد المجموعات المتساوية، أو نقسم طرفي المعادلة على المعامل.

$7k=91\Rightarrow k=\frac{91}{7}$

1. المعامل 7 غير صفري، لذا نقسم الطرفين عليه.

2. نحسب خارج قسمة 91 على 7 فنحصل على 13.

$k=13$

$13$ بلا وحدة قياس

$7(13)=91$

لا تطرح المعامل بدلاً من القسمة عليه.$mw$,$mw$Divide the total by the number of equal groups, or divide both sides by the coefficient.

$7k=91\Rightarrow k=\frac{91}{7}$

1. The coefficient seven is nonzero, so divide both sides by it.

2. Compute 91 divided by seven to get 13.

$k=13$

$13$ Dimensionless

$7(13)=91$

Do not subtract the coefficient instead of dividing by it.$mw$),
(707,692,$mw$12B41830682E97F390F0D638244282D546DB76DD4308CB3635F812F95F557BD0$mw$,$mw$61aaa3f2b687b135a6ea9955c581416d$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":692,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":2,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"إيجاد المقسوم المجهول باستخدام الضرب","TitleEn":"Find an unknown dividend by multiplication","QuestionTextAr":"إذا كان x ÷ 5 = 12، فما قيمة x؟","QuestionTextEn":"If x ÷ 5 = 12, what is x?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: الضرب يعكس القسمة؛ إذا كان س ÷ 5 = 12 فإننا نضرب الطرفين في 5. بالتعويض س = 12 × 5 = 60. التحقق: 60 ÷ 5 = 12، لذا القيمة المطلوبة 60.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Multiplication reverses division. For x ÷ 5 = 12, multiply both sides by 5: x = 12 × 5 = 60. Check: 60 ÷ 5 = 12, so x is 60.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2821,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"17","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2822,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"50","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2823,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2824,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"65","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"ما العملية العكسية للقسمة؟","En":"Which operation reverses division?"},{"Ar":"نفّذ العملية نفسها على طرفي المعادلة.","En":"Apply the same operation to both sides."}],"Title":{"Ar":"إيجاد المقسوم المجهول باستخدام الضرب","En":"Find an unknown dividend by multiplication"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"17","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"17 ناتج جمع 12 و5، وليس عكس القسمة.","En":"Seventeen adds 12 and five instead of undoing division."}},{"LatexCode":"50","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"50/5=10 وليس 12.","En":"50/5=10, not 12."}},{"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"65","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"65/5=13 وليس 12.","En":"65/5=13, not 12."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"إذا كان x ÷ 5 = 12، فما قيمة x؟","En":"If x ÷ 5 = 12, what is x?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نضرب طرفي المعادلة في المقسوم عليه لعزل المجهول.","En":"Multiply both sides by the divisor to isolate the unknown."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"القسمة على 5 تُعكس بالضرب في 5.","En":"Division by five is undone by multiplication by five."},{"Ar":"نضرب الطرفين في 5 ثم نحسب حاصل الضرب.","En":"Multiply both sides by five and evaluate."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$60$","En":"$60$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تجمع المقسوم عليه مع خارج القسمة.","En":"Do not add the divisor to the quotient."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac{x}{a}=b\\Rightarrow x=ab,\\quad a\\ne0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=12\\times5=60$","En":"$x=12\\times5=60$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$60/5=12$","En":"$60/5=12$"}},"TrackIds":[4],"CategoryId":2,"PrimarySkillId":9,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"ما العملية العكسية للقسمة؟","En":"Which operation reverses division?"},{"Ar":"نفّذ العملية نفسها على طرفي المعادلة.","En":"Apply the same operation to both sides."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نضرب طرفي المعادلة في المقسوم عليه لعزل المجهول.","En":"Multiply both sides by the divisor to isolate the unknown."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"القسمة على 5 تُعكس بالضرب في 5.","En":"Division by five is undone by multiplication by five."},{"Ar":"نضرب الطرفين في 5 ثم نحسب حاصل الضرب.","En":"Multiply both sides by five and evaluate."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$60$","En":"$60$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تجمع المقسوم عليه مع خارج القسمة.","En":"Do not add the divisor to the quotient."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac{x}{a}=b\\Rightarrow x=ab,\\quad a\\ne0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=12\\times5=60$","En":"$x=12\\times5=60$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$60/5=12$","En":"$60/5=12$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"17 ناتج جمع 12 و5، وليس عكس القسمة.","En":"Seventeen adds 12 and five instead of undoing division."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"50/5=10 وليس 12.","En":"50/5=10, not 12."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"65/5=13 وليس 12.","En":"65/5=13, not 12."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نضرب طرفي المعادلة في المقسوم عليه لعزل المجهول.

$\frac{x}{a}=b\Rightarrow x=ab,\quad a\ne0$

1. القسمة على 5 تُعكس بالضرب في 5.

2. نضرب الطرفين في 5 ثم نحسب حاصل الضرب.

$x=12\times5=60$

$60$ بلا وحدة قياس

$60/5=12$

لا تجمع المقسوم عليه مع خارج القسمة.$mw$,$mw$Multiply both sides by the divisor to isolate the unknown.

$\frac{x}{a}=b\Rightarrow x=ab,\quad a\ne0$

1. Division by five is undone by multiplication by five.

2. Multiply both sides by five and evaluate.

$x=12\times5=60$

$60$ Dimensionless

$60/5=12$

Do not add the divisor to the quotient.$mw$),
(708,693,$mw$02B6992D0733D393F86FB923B441BA451E279AB3C8A8083171512BA8109B2542$mw$,$mw$756dc4f42dbee51743ab7b749baaa830$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":693,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":21,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"استخدام مقياس موحد لتحويل كسر إلى مقام معلوم","TitleEn":"Scale equivalent fractions to a given denominator","QuestionTextAr":"أكمل الكسر المكافئ: 3/5 = x/20. ما قيمة x؟","QuestionTextEn":"Complete the equivalent fraction: 3/5 = x/20. Find x.","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: الكسور المتكافئة تنتج عند ضرب البسط والمقام في العامل نفسه غير الصفري. في 3/5 = س/20 نضرب المقام 5 في 4 ليصبح 20، لذلك نضرب البسط 3 في 4 أيضاً: س = 3 × 4 = 12. التحقق: 12/20 = 3/5.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Equivalent fractions multiply numerator and denominator by the same nonzero factor. In 3/5 = x/20, the denominator 5 becomes 20 by multiplying by 4. Therefore x = 3 × 4 = 12; check 12/20 = 3/5.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2825,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"8","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2826,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2827,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"15","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2828,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"18","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"ابحث عن معامل التكبير في المقام.","En":"Find the scaling factor in the denominator."},{"Ar":"اضرب البسط في معامل التكبير نفسه.","En":"Multiply the numerator by the same scaling factor."}],"Title":{"Ar":"استخدام مقياس موحد لتحويل كسر إلى مقام معلوم","En":"Scale equivalent fractions to a given denominator"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"8","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"5×8=40 وليس 3×20=60.","En":"5×8=40, not 3×20=60."}},{"LatexCode":"12","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"15","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"5×15=75 وليس 60.","En":"5×15=75, not 60."}},{"LatexCode":"18","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"5×18=90 وليس 60.","En":"5×18=90, not 60."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"أكمل الكسر المكافئ: 3/5 = x/20. ما قيمة x؟","En":"Complete the equivalent fraction: 3/5 = x/20. Find x."},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الكسور المتكافئة تنتج من ضرب البسط والمقام في العدد غير الصفري نفسه.","En":"Equivalent fractions multiply numerator and denominator by the same nonzero factor."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المقام 5 صار 20 بالضرب في 4.","En":"The denominator five becomes twenty by multiplying by four."},{"Ar":"نضرب البسط 3 في العامل نفسه ليبقى الكسر مكافئاً.","En":"Multiply numerator three by the same factor to preserve equivalence."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$12$","En":"$12$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تضرب المقام وحده وتترك البسط.","En":"Do not scale only the denominator."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{ka}{kb},\\quad bk\\ne0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=3\\times4=12$","En":"$x=3\\times4=12$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$12/20=3/5$","En":"$12/20=3/5$"}},"TrackIds":[4],"CategoryId":21,"PrimarySkillId":96,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"ابحث عن معامل التكبير في المقام.","En":"Find the scaling factor in the denominator."},{"Ar":"اضرب البسط في معامل التكبير نفسه.","En":"Multiply the numerator by the same scaling factor."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الكسور المتكافئة تنتج من ضرب البسط والمقام في العدد غير الصفري نفسه.","En":"Equivalent fractions multiply numerator and denominator by the same nonzero factor."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المقام 5 صار 20 بالضرب في 4.","En":"The denominator five becomes twenty by multiplying by four."},{"Ar":"نضرب البسط 3 في العامل نفسه ليبقى الكسر مكافئاً.","En":"Multiply numerator three by the same factor to preserve equivalence."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$12$","En":"$12$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تضرب المقام وحده وتترك البسط.","En":"Do not scale only the denominator."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{ka}{kb},\\quad bk\\ne0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=3\\times4=12$","En":"$x=3\\times4=12$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$12/20=3/5$","En":"$12/20=3/5$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"5×8=40 وليس 3×20=60.","En":"5×8=40, not 3×20=60."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"5×15=75 وليس 60.","En":"5×15=75, not 60."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"5×18=90 وليس 60.","En":"5×18=90, not 60."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الكسور المتكافئة تنتج من ضرب البسط والمقام في العدد غير الصفري نفسه.

$\frac{a}{b}=\frac{ka}{kb},\quad bk\ne0$

1. المقام 5 صار 20 بالضرب في 4.

2. نضرب البسط 3 في العامل نفسه ليبقى الكسر مكافئاً.

$x=3\times4=12$

$12$ بلا وحدة قياس

$12/20=3/5$

لا تضرب المقام وحده وتترك البسط.$mw$,$mw$Equivalent fractions multiply numerator and denominator by the same nonzero factor.

$\frac{a}{b}=\frac{ka}{kb},\quad bk\ne0$

1. The denominator five becomes twenty by multiplying by four.

2. Multiply numerator three by the same factor to preserve equivalence.

$x=3\times4=12$

$12$ Dimensionless

$12/20=3/5$

Do not scale only the denominator.$mw$),
(709,694,$mw$52831F066FEBA851D23C97529C9FA1A066B5289F52F63B7ACEDB78E42623B0D7$mw$,$mw$ec31a53d4f62ca8661da2fffcd37c231$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":694,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":21,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تبسيط كسر بالقاسم المشترك الأكبر","TitleEn":"Reduce a fraction using common factors","QuestionTextAr":"ما الصورة المبسطة للكسر 14/21؟","QuestionTextEn":"What is the simplest form of 14/21?","DetailedSolutionAr":"القانون المستخدم: تبسيط كسر يتم بقسمة البسط والمقام على القاسم المشترك الأكبر. القاسم المشترك الأكبر للعددين 14 و21 هو 7؛ إذن 14/21 = (14 ÷ 7)/(21 ÷ 7) = 2/3. لا يوجد قاسم مشترك أكبر من 1 بين 2 و3.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Simplify a fraction by dividing numerator and denominator by their greatest common divisor. gcd(14, 21) = 7, so 14/21 = (14 ÷ 7)/(21 ÷ 7) = 2/3. Since 2 and 3 share no factor greater than 1, this is simplest form.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2829,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2830,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac23","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2831,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"\\frac34","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2832,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\frac{7}{10}","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"ابحث عن قاسم مشترك للبسط والمقام.","En":"Look for a common factor of numerator and denominator."},{"Ar":"استخدم أكبر قاسم مشترك لتصل إلى أبسط صورة.","En":"Use the greatest common factor to reach simplest form."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تبسيط كسر بالقاسم المشترك الأكبر","En":"Reduce a fraction using common factors"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"14×2=28 ولا يساوي 21×1.","En":"14×2=28 differs from 21×1."}},{"LatexCode":"\\frac23","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"\\frac34","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"14×4=56 ولا يساوي 21×3=63.","En":"14×4=56 differs from 21×3=63."}},{"LatexCode":"\\frac{7}{10}","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"14×10=140 ولا يساوي 21×7=147.","En":"14×10=140 differs from 21×7=147."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"ما الصورة المبسطة للكسر 14/21؟","En":"What is the simplest form of 14/21?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"تبسيط الكسر بقسمة البسط والمقام على قاسم مشترك غير صفري.","En":"Reduce a fraction by dividing numerator and denominator by the same nonzero common factor."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"14=2×7 و21=3×7؛ القاسم المشترك الأكبر 7.","En":"14=2×7 and 21=3×7, so the greatest common factor is seven."},{"Ar":"نقسم البسط والمقام على 7 فنحصل على 2 و3.","En":"Divide both terms by seven to obtain two and three."},{"Ar":"لا يوجد قاسم مشترك أكبر من 1 بين 2 و3.","En":"Two and three have no common factor greater than one."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac23$","En":"$\\frac23$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تختصر البسط والمقام بعاملين مختلفين.","En":"Do not reduce numerator and denominator by different factors."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac ab=\\frac{a/d}{b/d},\\quad bd\\ne0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac{14/7}{21/7}=\\frac23$","En":"$\\frac{14/7}{21/7}=\\frac23$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$14\\cdot3=21\\cdot2=42$","En":"$14\\cdot3=21\\cdot2=42$"}},"TrackIds":[4],"CategoryId":21,"PrimarySkillId":96,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"ابحث عن قاسم مشترك للبسط والمقام.","En":"Look for a common factor of numerator and denominator."},{"Ar":"استخدم أكبر قاسم مشترك لتصل إلى أبسط صورة.","En":"Use the greatest common factor to reach simplest form."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"تبسيط الكسر بقسمة البسط والمقام على قاسم مشترك غير صفري.","En":"Reduce a fraction by dividing numerator and denominator by the same nonzero common factor."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"14=2×7 و21=3×7؛ القاسم المشترك الأكبر 7.","En":"14=2×7 and 21=3×7, so the greatest common factor is seven."},{"Ar":"نقسم البسط والمقام على 7 فنحصل على 2 و3.","En":"Divide both terms by seven to obtain two and three."},{"Ar":"لا يوجد قاسم مشترك أكبر من 1 بين 2 و3.","En":"Two and three have no common factor greater than one."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac23$","En":"$\\frac23$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تختصر البسط والمقام بعاملين مختلفين.","En":"Do not reduce numerator and denominator by different factors."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac ab=\\frac{a/d}{b/d},\\quad bd\\ne0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac{14/7}{21/7}=\\frac23$","En":"$\\frac{14/7}{21/7}=\\frac23$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$14\\cdot3=21\\cdot2=42$","En":"$14\\cdot3=21\\cdot2=42$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"14×2=28 ولا يساوي 21×1.","En":"14×2=28 differs from 21×1."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"14×4=56 ولا يساوي 21×3=63.","En":"14×4=56 differs from 21×3=63."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"14×10=140 ولا يساوي 21×7=147.","En":"14×10=140 differs from 21×7=147."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$تبسيط الكسر بقسمة البسط والمقام على قاسم مشترك غير صفري.

$\frac ab=\frac{a/d}{b/d},\quad bd\ne0$

1. 14=2×7 و21=3×7؛ القاسم المشترك الأكبر 7.

2. نقسم البسط والمقام على 7 فنحصل على 2 و3.

3. لا يوجد قاسم مشترك أكبر من 1 بين 2 و3.

$\frac{14/7}{21/7}=\frac23$

$\frac23$ بلا وحدة قياس

$14\cdot3=21\cdot2=42$

لا تختصر البسط والمقام بعاملين مختلفين.$mw$,$mw$Reduce a fraction by dividing numerator and denominator by the same nonzero common factor.

$\frac ab=\frac{a/d}{b/d},\quad bd\ne0$

1. 14=2×7 and 21=3×7, so the greatest common factor is seven.

2. Divide both terms by seven to obtain two and three.

3. Two and three have no common factor greater than one.

$\frac{14/7}{21/7}=\frac23$

$\frac23$ Dimensionless

$14\cdot3=21\cdot2=42$

Do not reduce numerator and denominator by different factors.$mw$),
(710,695,$mw$1D5185AAAB167938E6556BB300A602CE472CC6D28D4D95DD078356FFCA286F03$mw$,$mw$0fe1c503d262d5b0a4e98ada2c5890fc$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":695,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":21,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"ربط الكسر المكافئ بالتمثيل العشري","TitleEn":"Connect decimal and fraction representations","QuestionTextAr":"أي كسر يساوي العدد العشري 0.75 بالضبط؟","QuestionTextEn":"Which fraction is exactly equal to the decimal 0.75?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: العدد العشري ذو منزلتين بعد الفاصلة يكتب على مقام 100. نحول 0.75 إلى 75/100، ثم نقسم البسط والمقام على 25: (75 ÷ 25)/(100 ÷ 25) = 3/4. إذن 0.75 يساوي ثلاثة أرباع تماماً.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: A decimal with two places can be written over 100. Thus 0.75 = 75/100. Divide both terms by 25: (75 ÷ 25)/(100 ÷ 25) = 3/4. Therefore 0.75 equals three quarters exactly.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2833,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac14","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2834,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac23","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2835,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"\\frac34","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2836,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\frac45","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"اكتب العدد العشري على صورة كسر مقامه 100.","En":"Write the decimal as a fraction over 100."},{"Ar":"اختصر الكسر بقاسم مشترك للبسط والمقام.","En":"Simplify by a common factor."}],"Title":{"Ar":"ربط الكسر المكافئ بالتمثيل العشري","En":"Connect decimal and fraction representations"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"\\frac14","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1/4=0.25 وليس 0.75.","En":"1/4=0.25, not 0.75."}},{"LatexCode":"\\frac23","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2/3 أقل من 3/4 لأن 8<9 في مقام 12.","En":"2/3 is below 3/4 because 8<9 over denominator 12."}},{"LatexCode":"\\frac34","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"\\frac45","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"4/5=0.8 وليس 0.75.","En":"4/5=0.8, not 0.75."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"أي كسر يساوي العدد العشري 0.75 بالضبط؟","En":"Which fraction is exactly equal to the decimal 0.75?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"كل منزلتين عشريتين تمثلان أجزاء من مئة.","En":"Two decimal places represent hundredths."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"0.75 تعني 75 جزءاً من مئة.","En":"0.75 means 75 hundredths."},{"Ar":"نقسم البسط والمقام على 25 لنحصل على 3/4.","En":"Divide both numerator and denominator by 25 to get 3/4."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac34$","En":"$\\frac34$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستعمل مقام 10 لعدد له منزلتان عشريتان.","En":"Do not use denominator ten for a two-place decimal."},"FormulaLatex":"0.75=\\frac{75}{100}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac{75}{100}=\\frac34$","En":"$\\frac{75}{100}=\\frac34$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$3\\div4=0.75$","En":"$3\\div4=0.75$"}},"TrackIds":[5],"CategoryId":21,"PrimarySkillId":96,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"اكتب العدد العشري على صورة كسر مقامه 100.","En":"Write the decimal as a fraction over 100."},{"Ar":"اختصر الكسر بقاسم مشترك للبسط والمقام.","En":"Simplify by a common factor."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"كل منزلتين عشريتين تمثلان أجزاء من مئة.","En":"Two decimal places represent hundredths."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"0.75 تعني 75 جزءاً من مئة.","En":"0.75 means 75 hundredths."},{"Ar":"نقسم البسط والمقام على 25 لنحصل على 3/4.","En":"Divide both numerator and denominator by 25 to get 3/4."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac34$","En":"$\\frac34$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستعمل مقام 10 لعدد له منزلتان عشريتان.","En":"Do not use denominator ten for a two-place decimal."},"FormulaLatex":"0.75=\\frac{75}{100}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac{75}{100}=\\frac34$","En":"$\\frac{75}{100}=\\frac34$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$3\\div4=0.75$","En":"$3\\div4=0.75$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1/4=0.25 وليس 0.75.","En":"1/4=0.25, not 0.75."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2/3 أقل من 3/4 لأن 8<9 في مقام 12.","En":"2/3 is below 3/4 because 8<9 over denominator 12."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"4/5=0.8 وليس 0.75.","En":"4/5=0.8, not 0.75."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$كل منزلتين عشريتين تمثلان أجزاء من مئة.

$0.75=\frac{75}{100}$

1. 0.75 تعني 75 جزءاً من مئة.

2. نقسم البسط والمقام على 25 لنحصل على 3/4.

$\frac{75}{100}=\frac34$

$\frac34$ بلا وحدة قياس

$3\div4=0.75$

لا تستعمل مقام 10 لعدد له منزلتان عشريتان.$mw$,$mw$Two decimal places represent hundredths.

$0.75=\frac{75}{100}$

1. 0.75 means 75 hundredths.

2. Divide both numerator and denominator by 25 to get 3/4.

$\frac{75}{100}=\frac34$

$\frac34$ Dimensionless

$3\div4=0.75$

Do not use denominator ten for a two-place decimal.$mw$),
(711,696,$mw$799D17F183105AE438AF2A1686C6A9F750827D5916394EA75AC19AD764D95EF7$mw$,$mw$4b964594b5c2ca3c2e20280606b70f33$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":696,"StageId":1,"CategoryId":21,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تصحيح اعتقاد أن زيادة البسط والمقام بالقيمة نفسها تحفظ التكافؤ","TitleEn":"Challenge the add-one numerator-and-denominator misconception","QuestionTextAr":"يقول طالب إن 2/3 و3/4 كسران متكافئان لأننا زدنا 1 للبسط والمقام. ما المقارنة الصحيحة؟","QuestionTextEn":"A pupil says 2/3 and 3/4 are equivalent because 1 was added to both numerator and denominator. Which comparison is correct?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: كسران متكافئان يجب أن يكون لهما القيمة نفسها، ولا يكفي جمع 1 للبسط والمقام. نقارن 2/3 و3/4 بالضرب التبادلي: 2 × 4 = 8 و3 × 3 = 9، وبما أن 8 < 9 إذن 2/3 < 3/4. كلام التلميذ غير صحيح.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Equivalent fractions must have the same value; adding 1 to both numerator and denominator does not preserve value in general. Cross-multiply: 2 × 4 = 8 and 3 × 3 = 9. Since 8 < 9, we have 2/3 < 3/4, not equality.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2837,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac23=\\frac34","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2838,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac23>\\frac34","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2839,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"\\frac23<\\frac34","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2840,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\frac23=\\frac24","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في قيمة الكسر لا في الفرق بين البسط والمقام.","En":"Think about the fraction's value, not the difference between its terms."},{"Ar":"اضرب بسط كل كسر في مقام الآخر وقارن.","En":"Cross multiply and compare the products."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تصحيح اعتقاد أن زيادة البسط والمقام بالقيمة نفسها تحفظ التكافؤ","En":"Challenge the add-one numerator-and-denominator misconception"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"\\frac23=\\frac34","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"في مقام 12، البسطان 8 و9 مختلفان.","En":"With denominator 12, the numerators eight and nine differ."}},{"LatexCode":"\\frac23>\\frac34","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"8 أصغر من 9، لذلك اتجاه المقارنة معكوس.","En":"Eight is smaller than nine, so the comparison is reversed."}},{"LatexCode":"\\frac23<\\frac34","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"\\frac23=\\frac24","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2/4=1/2=6/12، وليس 8/12.","En":"2/4=1/2=6/12, not 8/12."}}],"StageId":1,"Question":{"Ar":"يقول طالب إن 2/3 و3/4 كسران متكافئان لأننا زدنا 1 للبسط والمقام. ما المقارنة الصحيحة؟","En":"A pupil says 2/3 and 3/4 are equivalent because 1 was added to both numerator and denominator. Which comparison is correct?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الكسور المتكافئة تنتج بضرب أو قسمة الطرفين بالعامل نفسه، لا بإضافة العدد نفسه.","En":"Equivalent fractions scale both terms by the same factor; adding the same number does not preserve the ratio."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نوحد المقامين إلى 12.","En":"Use common denominator 12."},{"Ar":"$\\frac23=\\frac8{12}$ و$\\frac34=\\frac9{12}$.","En":"$\\frac23=\\frac8{12}$ and $\\frac34=\\frac9{12}$."},{"Ar":"بما أن 8 أصغر من 9، فالكسر الأول أصغر.","En":"Since eight is below nine, the first fraction is smaller."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac23<\\frac34$","En":"$\\frac23<\\frac34$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"إضافة العدد نفسه للبسط والمقام لا تحافظ على قيمة الكسر عموماً.","En":"Adding the same number to numerator and denominator does not generally preserve a fraction's value."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac ab<\\frac cd\\iff ad<bc,\\quad b,d>0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$2\\cdot4=8<9=3\\cdot3$","En":"$2\\cdot4=8<9=3\\cdot3$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\frac8{12}<\\frac9{12}$","En":"$\\frac8{12}<\\frac9{12}$"}},"TrackIds":[4],"CategoryId":21,"PrimarySkillId":96,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"فكر في قيمة الكسر لا في الفرق بين البسط والمقام.","En":"Think about the fraction's value, not the difference between its terms."},{"Ar":"اضرب بسط كل كسر في مقام الآخر وقارن.","En":"Cross multiply and compare the products."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الكسور المتكافئة تنتج بضرب أو قسمة الطرفين بالعامل نفسه، لا بإضافة العدد نفسه.","En":"Equivalent fractions scale both terms by the same factor; adding the same number does not preserve the ratio."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نوحد المقامين إلى 12.","En":"Use common denominator 12."},{"Ar":"$\\frac23=\\frac8{12}$ و$\\frac34=\\frac9{12}$.","En":"$\\frac23=\\frac8{12}$ and $\\frac34=\\frac9{12}$."},{"Ar":"بما أن 8 أصغر من 9، فالكسر الأول أصغر.","En":"Since eight is below nine, the first fraction is smaller."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac23<\\frac34$","En":"$\\frac23<\\frac34$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"إضافة العدد نفسه للبسط والمقام لا تحافظ على قيمة الكسر عموماً.","En":"Adding the same number to numerator and denominator does not generally preserve a fraction's value."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac ab<\\frac cd\\iff ad<bc,\\quad b,d>0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$2\\cdot4=8<9=3\\cdot3$","En":"$2\\cdot4=8<9=3\\cdot3$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\frac8{12}<\\frac9{12}$","En":"$\\frac8{12}<\\frac9{12}$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"في مقام 12، البسطان 8 و9 مختلفان.","En":"With denominator 12, the numerators eight and nine differ."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"8 أصغر من 9، لذلك اتجاه المقارنة معكوس.","En":"Eight is smaller than nine, so the comparison is reversed."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2/4=1/2=6/12، وليس 8/12.","En":"2/4=1/2=6/12, not 8/12."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الكسور المتكافئة تنتج بضرب أو قسمة الطرفين بالعامل نفسه، لا بإضافة العدد نفسه.

$\frac ab<\frac cd\iff ad<bc,\quad b,d>0$

1. نوحد المقامين إلى 12.

2. $\frac23=\frac8{12}$ و$\frac34=\frac9{12}$.

3. بما أن 8 أصغر من 9، فالكسر الأول أصغر.

$2\cdot4=8<9=3\cdot3$

$\frac23<\frac34$ بلا وحدة قياس

$\frac8{12}<\frac9{12}$

إضافة العدد نفسه للبسط والمقام لا تحافظ على قيمة الكسر عموماً.$mw$,$mw$Equivalent fractions scale both terms by the same factor; adding the same number does not preserve the ratio.

$\frac ab<\frac cd\iff ad<bc,\quad b,d>0$

1. Use common denominator 12.

2. $\frac23=\frac8{12}$ and $\frac34=\frac9{12}$.

3. Since eight is below nine, the first fraction is smaller.

$2\cdot4=8<9=3\cdot3$

$\frac23<\frac34$ Dimensionless

$\frac8{12}<\frac9{12}$

Adding the same number to numerator and denominator does not generally preserve a fraction's value.$mw$),
(712,697,$mw$BB7DBE2730A18F636DC60A54F06B563361F21784C561C66CBC43BDEA676E8BF1$mw$,$mw$b7b6609093a9bf35a295119065d72b16$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":697,"StageId":2,"CategoryId":8,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"إيجاد زاويتي قاعدة مثلث متساوي الساقين","TitleEn":"Find base angles in an isosceles triangle","QuestionTextAr":"زاوية رأس مثلث متساوي الساقين 40°. كم قياس كل زاوية عند القاعدة؟","QuestionTextEn":"The apex angle of an isosceles triangle is 40°. What is each base angle?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: زاويتا القاعدة في المثلث متساوي الساقين متساويتان. مجموع زوايا أي مثلث 180°. بوجود زاوية رأس 40° يكون مجموع زاويتي القاعدة 180° − 40° = 140°. إذن قياس كل منهما = 140° ÷ 2 = 70°.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal, and all triangle angles sum to 180°. With a 40° apex, the two base angles sum to 180° − 40° = 140°, so each equals 140° ÷ 2 = 70°.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2841,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"40","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2842,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2843,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"70","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2844,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"80","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"تذكر مجموع الزوايا وتساوي زاويتي القاعدة.","En":"Recall the angle sum and equal base angles."},{"Ar":"اطرح زاوية الرأس من المجموع ثم اقسم الباقي بالتساوي.","En":"Subtract the apex angle from the total and split the remainder equally."}],"Title":{"Ar":"إيجاد زاويتي قاعدة مثلث متساوي الساقين","En":"Find base angles in an isosceles triangle"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"40","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"40+40+40=120 لا 180.","En":"40+40+40=120, not 180."}},{"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"40+60+60=160 لا 180.","En":"40+60+60=160, not 180."}},{"LatexCode":"70","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"80","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"40+80+80=200 لا 180.","En":"40+80+80=200, not 180."}}],"StageId":2,"Question":{"Ar":"زاوية رأس مثلث متساوي الساقين 40°. كم قياس كل زاوية عند القاعدة؟","En":"The apex angle of an isosceles triangle is 40°. What is each base angle?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"زاويتا قاعدة المثلث المتساوي الساقين متساويتان.","En":"The base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"زاويتا القاعدة متساويتان، ومجموع زوايا المثلث 180 درجة.","En":"Base angles are equal, and a triangle's angles sum to 180 degrees."},{"Ar":"نطرح 40 من 180، فيبقى 140 للزاويتين.","En":"Subtract 40 from 180, leaving 140 for both angles."},{"Ar":"نقسم 140 على اثنين فنحصل على 70 لكل زاوية.","En":"Divide 140 by two to obtain 70 per angle."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$70$","En":"$70$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط زاوية الرأس بزاويتي القاعدة.","En":"Do not confuse the apex with the base angles."},"FormulaLatex":"2B+40^\\circ=180^\\circ","Substitution":{"Ar":"$B=140^\\circ/2=70^\\circ$","En":"$B=140^\\circ/2=70^\\circ$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$40+70+70=180$","En":"$40+70+70=180$"}},"TrackIds":[7],"CategoryId":8,"PrimarySkillId":35,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"تذكر مجموع الزوايا وتساوي زاويتي القاعدة.","En":"Recall the angle sum and equal base angles."},{"Ar":"اطرح زاوية الرأس من المجموع ثم اقسم الباقي بالتساوي.","En":"Subtract the apex angle from the total and split the remainder equally."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"زاويتا قاعدة المثلث المتساوي الساقين متساويتان.","En":"The base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"زاويتا القاعدة متساويتان، ومجموع زوايا المثلث 180 درجة.","En":"Base angles are equal, and a triangle's angles sum to 180 degrees."},{"Ar":"نطرح 40 من 180، فيبقى 140 للزاويتين.","En":"Subtract 40 from 180, leaving 140 for both angles."},{"Ar":"نقسم 140 على اثنين فنحصل على 70 لكل زاوية.","En":"Divide 140 by two to obtain 70 per angle."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$70$","En":"$70$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط زاوية الرأس بزاويتي القاعدة.","En":"Do not confuse the apex with the base angles."},"FormulaLatex":"2B+40^\\circ=180^\\circ","Substitution":{"Ar":"$B=140^\\circ/2=70^\\circ$","En":"$B=140^\\circ/2=70^\\circ$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$40+70+70=180$","En":"$40+70+70=180$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"40+40+40=120 لا 180.","En":"40+40+40=120, not 180."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"40+60+60=160 لا 180.","En":"40+60+60=160, not 180."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"40+80+80=200 لا 180.","En":"40+80+80=200, not 180."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$زاويتا قاعدة المثلث المتساوي الساقين متساويتان.

$2B+40^\circ=180^\circ$

1. زاويتا القاعدة متساويتان، ومجموع زوايا المثلث 180 درجة.

2. نطرح 40 من 180، فيبقى 140 للزاويتين.

3. نقسم 140 على اثنين فنحصل على 70 لكل زاوية.

$B=140^\circ/2=70^\circ$

$70$ درجة

$40+70+70=180$

لا تخلط زاوية الرأس بزاويتي القاعدة.$mw$,$mw$The base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal.

$2B+40^\circ=180^\circ$

1. Base angles are equal, and a triangle's angles sum to 180 degrees.

2. Subtract 40 from 180, leaving 140 for both angles.

3. Divide 140 by two to obtain 70 per angle.

$B=140^\circ/2=70^\circ$

$70$ Degrees

$40+70+70=180$

Do not confuse the apex with the base angles.$mw$),
(714,699,$mw$EC8347C6E7EA79C9550480EC7516BEE63BC1D4DC536C86A879D9D5914F80B27B$mw$,$mw$2f1a19933dbfe84a103a6afc21659907$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":699,"StageId":2,"CategoryId":8,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"استنتاج الزاوية الحادة الأخرى في مثلث قائم","TitleEn":"Find the remaining acute angle in a right triangle","QuestionTextAr":"في مثلث قائم إحدى الزاويتين الحادتين 35°. ما قياس الزاوية الحادة الأخرى؟","QuestionTextEn":"In a right triangle, one acute angle is 35°. What is the other acute angle?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: إحدى زوايا المثلث القائم 90° ومجموع الزوايا الثلاث 180°، لذا مجموع الزاويتين الحادتين = 90°. إذا كانت إحداهما 35° فإن الأخرى = 90° − 35° = 55°. التحقق: 90° + 35° + 55° = 180°.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: A right triangle has one 90° angle, so its two acute angles total 90°. When one acute angle is 35°, the other equals 90° − 35° = 55°. Check: 90° + 35° + 55° = 180°.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2849,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"35","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2850,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"45","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2851,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"55","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2852,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"65","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"المثلث يحتوي زاوية قائمة.","En":"The triangle contains a right angle."},{"Ar":"اطرح الزاوية الحادة المعطاة من مجموع الزاويتين الحادتين.","En":"Subtract the known acute angle from the acute-angle sum."}],"Title":{"Ar":"استنتاج الزاوية الحادة الأخرى في مثلث قائم","En":"Find the remaining acute angle in a right triangle"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"35","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35+35+90=160 وليس 180.","En":"35+35+90=160, not 180."}},{"LatexCode":"45","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35+45+90=170 وليس 180.","En":"35+45+90=170, not 180."}},{"LatexCode":"55","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"65","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35+65+90=190 وليس 180.","En":"35+65+90=190, not 180."}}],"StageId":2,"Question":{"Ar":"في مثلث قائم إحدى الزاويتين الحادتين 35°. ما قياس الزاوية الحادة الأخرى؟","En":"In a right triangle, one acute angle is 35°. What is the other acute angle?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الزاويتان الحادتان في المثلث القائم متتامتان.","En":"The acute angles in a right triangle are complementary."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الزاوية القائمة 90 درجة؛ تبقى 90 للزاويتين الحادتين.","En":"The right angle is 90 degrees, leaving 90 for the acute angles."},{"Ar":"نطرح 35 من 90 لنجد الزاوية الأخرى.","En":"Subtract 35 from 90 to find the other angle."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$55$","En":"$55$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تطرح 35 من 180 وحدها؛ احسب الزاوية القائمة أيضاً.","En":"Do not subtract only 35 from 180; account for the right angle."},"FormulaLatex":"A+B=90^\\circ","Substitution":{"Ar":"$B=90^\\circ-35^\\circ=55^\\circ$","En":"$B=90^\\circ-35^\\circ=55^\\circ$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$35+55+90=180$","En":"$35+55+90=180$"}},"TrackIds":[7],"CategoryId":8,"PrimarySkillId":35,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"المثلث يحتوي زاوية قائمة.","En":"The triangle contains a right angle."},{"Ar":"اطرح الزاوية الحادة المعطاة من مجموع الزاويتين الحادتين.","En":"Subtract the known acute angle from the acute-angle sum."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الزاويتان الحادتان في المثلث القائم متتامتان.","En":"The acute angles in a right triangle are complementary."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الزاوية القائمة 90 درجة؛ تبقى 90 للزاويتين الحادتين.","En":"The right angle is 90 degrees, leaving 90 for the acute angles."},{"Ar":"نطرح 35 من 90 لنجد الزاوية الأخرى.","En":"Subtract 35 from 90 to find the other angle."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$55$","En":"$55$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تطرح 35 من 180 وحدها؛ احسب الزاوية القائمة أيضاً.","En":"Do not subtract only 35 from 180; account for the right angle."},"FormulaLatex":"A+B=90^\\circ","Substitution":{"Ar":"$B=90^\\circ-35^\\circ=55^\\circ$","En":"$B=90^\\circ-35^\\circ=55^\\circ$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$35+55+90=180$","En":"$35+55+90=180$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35+35+90=160 وليس 180.","En":"35+35+90=160, not 180."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35+45+90=170 وليس 180.","En":"35+45+90=170, not 180."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35+65+90=190 وليس 180.","En":"35+65+90=190, not 180."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الزاويتان الحادتان في المثلث القائم متتامتان.

$A+B=90^\circ$

1. الزاوية القائمة 90 درجة؛ تبقى 90 للزاويتين الحادتين.

2. نطرح 35 من 90 لنجد الزاوية الأخرى.

$B=90^\circ-35^\circ=55^\circ$

$55$ درجة

$35+55+90=180$

لا تطرح 35 من 180 وحدها؛ احسب الزاوية القائمة أيضاً.$mw$,$mw$The acute angles in a right triangle are complementary.

$A+B=90^\circ$

1. The right angle is 90 degrees, leaving 90 for the acute angles.

2. Subtract 35 from 90 to find the other angle.

$B=90^\circ-35^\circ=55^\circ$

$55$ Degrees

$35+55+90=180$

Do not subtract only 35 from 180; account for the right angle.$mw$),
(715,700,$mw$BCA953960A840183F1D066A14C89A5025356E22A4CEF4D6647534F442F4B77C9$mw$,$mw$bdb98077d519a4824ebeaca7df8bd872$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":700,"StageId":2,"CategoryId":8,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تقسيم مجموع زوايا مثلث بنسبة معطاة","TitleEn":"Use a ratio to determine a triangle's largest angle","QuestionTextAr":"زوايا مثلث بنسبة 1 : 2 : 3. ما قياس أكبر زاوية فيه بالدرجات؟","QuestionTextEn":"A triangle's angles are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3. How many degrees is its largest angle?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: مجموع زوايا المثلث 180° والنسبة 1 : 2 : 3 تمثل ستة أجزاء متساوية. الجزء الواحد = 180° ÷ (1 + 2 + 3) = 30°. أكبر زاوية تمثل 3 أجزاء، لذلك 3 × 30° = 90°. الزوايا الثلاث هي 30° و60° و90°.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: A triangle's angles sum to 180°. A 1:2:3 ratio has 1 + 2 + 3 = 6 equal parts, so each part is 180° ÷ 6 = 30°. The largest angle has 3 parts: 3 × 30° = 90°. The angles are 30°, 60°, 90°.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2745,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"30","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2746,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2747,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"90","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2748,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"120","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"اجمع أجزاء نسبة الزوايا.","En":"Sum the angle ratio parts."},{"Ar":"احسب قيمة الجزء الواحد واضرب بأكبر عدد أجزاء.","En":"Find one part and multiply by the largest ratio term."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تقسيم مجموع زوايا مثلث بنسبة معطاة","En":"Use a ratio to determine a triangle's largest angle"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"30","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"30 قياس أصغر زاوية.","En":"Thirty is the smallest angle."}},{"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"60 قياس الزاوية الوسطى.","En":"Sixty is the middle angle."}},{"LatexCode":"90","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"120","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"لو كانت الكبرى 120 لكان المجموع 240، وهو مستحيل.","En":"If the largest were 120 the total would be 240, impossible."}}],"StageId":2,"Question":{"Ar":"زوايا مثلث بنسبة 1 : 2 : 3. ما قياس أكبر زاوية فيه بالدرجات؟","En":"A triangle's angles are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3. How many degrees is its largest angle?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"مجموع أجزاء نسبة زوايا المثلث يقابل 180 درجة.","En":"The total ratio parts of triangle angles represent 180 degrees."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نمثل الزوايا بـ x و2x و3x حيث x موجب.","En":"Represent the angles by x, 2x and 3x with positive x."},{"Ar":"مجموعها 6x=180، إذن x=30.","En":"Their sum is 6x=180, hence x=30."},{"Ar":"أكبر زاوية تساوي 3x=90.","En":"The largest is 3x=90."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$90$","En":"$90$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تتوقف عند قيمة الجزء الواحد؛ المطلوب ثلاثة أجزاء.","En":"Do not stop at one ratio unit; the question asks for three."},"FormulaLatex":"x+2x+3x=180^\\circ","Substitution":{"Ar":"$3(180/6)=90$","En":"$3(180/6)=90$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$30+60+90=180$","En":"$30+60+90=180$"}},"TrackIds":[8],"CategoryId":8,"PrimarySkillId":35,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"اجمع أجزاء نسبة الزوايا.","En":"Sum the angle ratio parts."},{"Ar":"احسب قيمة الجزء الواحد واضرب بأكبر عدد أجزاء.","En":"Find one part and multiply by the largest ratio term."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"مجموع أجزاء نسبة زوايا المثلث يقابل 180 درجة.","En":"The total ratio parts of triangle angles represent 180 degrees."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نمثل الزوايا بـ x و2x و3x حيث x موجب.","En":"Represent the angles by x, 2x and 3x with positive x."},{"Ar":"مجموعها 6x=180، إذن x=30.","En":"Their sum is 6x=180, hence x=30."},{"Ar":"أكبر زاوية تساوي 3x=90.","En":"The largest is 3x=90."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$90$","En":"$90$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تتوقف عند قيمة الجزء الواحد؛ المطلوب ثلاثة أجزاء.","En":"Do not stop at one ratio unit; the question asks for three."},"FormulaLatex":"x+2x+3x=180^\\circ","Substitution":{"Ar":"$3(180/6)=90$","En":"$3(180/6)=90$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$30+60+90=180$","En":"$30+60+90=180$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"30 قياس أصغر زاوية.","En":"Thirty is the smallest angle."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"60 قياس الزاوية الوسطى.","En":"Sixty is the middle angle."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"لو كانت الكبرى 120 لكان المجموع 240، وهو مستحيل.","En":"If the largest were 120 the total would be 240, impossible."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$مجموع أجزاء نسبة زوايا المثلث يقابل 180 درجة.

$x+2x+3x=180^\circ$

1. نمثل الزوايا بـ x و2x و3x حيث x موجب.

2. مجموعها 6x=180، إذن x=30.

3. أكبر زاوية تساوي 3x=90.

$3(180/6)=90$

$90$ درجة

$30+60+90=180$

لا تتوقف عند قيمة الجزء الواحد؛ المطلوب ثلاثة أجزاء.$mw$,$mw$The total ratio parts of triangle angles represent 180 degrees.

$x+2x+3x=180^\circ$

1. Represent the angles by x, 2x and 3x with positive x.

2. Their sum is 6x=180, hence x=30.

3. The largest is 3x=90.

$3(180/6)=90$

$90$ Degrees

$30+60+90=180$

Do not stop at one ratio unit; the question asks for three.$mw$),
(716,701,$mw$F50CBB8EB2922666BEA52EA5E5BABFEBD05FCD1B523401DEBA48605E1B96FCDB$mw$,$mw$142c217a15883c4355d20d2e941b8c08$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":701,"StageId":2,"CategoryId":8,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"حل معادلة من تساوي زاويتين متقابلتين بالرأس","TitleEn":"Solve an equation using vertically opposite angles","QuestionTextAr":"زاويتان متقابلتان بالرأس قياساهما (x + 20)° و(3x − 40)°. ما x؟","QuestionTextEn":"Vertically opposite angles measure (x + 20)° and (3x − 40)°. Find x.","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: الزوايا المتقابلة بالرأس متساوية. نساوي التعبيرين: س + 20 = 3س − 40. بإضافة 40 وطرح س من الطرفين نحصل على 60 = 2س، وبالتالي س = 60 ÷ 2 = 30. التحقق: 30 + 20 = 3 × 30 − 40 = 50°.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Vertically opposite angles are equal. Set x + 20 = 3x − 40. Rearrange to obtain 60 = 2x, hence x = 30. Check the two angle measures: 30 + 20 = 50° and 3 × 30 − 40 = 50°.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2749,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"20","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2750,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"30","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2751,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"40","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2752,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"استعمل تساوي الزاويتين المتقابلتين.","En":"Use equality of vertical angles."},{"Ar":"ساو التعبيرين ثم اجمع حدود المجهول في طرف.","En":"Set the expressions equal, then collect variable terms."}],"Title":{"Ar":"حل معادلة من تساوي زاويتين متقابلتين بالرأس","En":"Solve an equation using vertically opposite angles"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"20","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"عند x=20 القياسان 40 و20 غير متساويين.","En":"At x=20 the measures are 40 and 20, unequal."}},{"LatexCode":"30","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null},{"LatexCode":"40","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"عند x=40 القياسان 60 و80.","En":"At x=40 the measures are 60 and 80."}},{"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"عند x=60 القياسان 80 و140.","En":"At x=60 the measures are 80 and 140."}}],"StageId":2,"Question":{"Ar":"زاويتان متقابلتان بالرأس قياساهما (x + 20)° و(3x − 40)°. ما x؟","En":"Vertically opposite angles measure (x + 20)° and (3x − 40)°. Find x."},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الزاويتان المتقابلتان بالرأس متساويتان.","En":"Vertically opposite angles are equal."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الزاويتان المتقابلتان بالرأس متساويتان.","En":"Vertical angles have equal measures."},{"Ar":"ننقل الحدود: 20+40=3x−x.","En":"Rearrange: 20+40=3x−x."},{"Ar":"نقسم 60 على 2 فنحصل على x=30.","En":"Divide 60 by two to find x=30."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$30$","En":"$30$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تجعل مجموع الزاويتين المتقابلتين 180؛ هذا للمجاورتين على مستقيم.","En":"Do not set vertical angles to sum to 180; that is for adjacent angles forming a straight line."},"FormulaLatex":"x+20=3x-40","Substitution":{"Ar":"$2x=60\\Rightarrow x=30$","En":"$2x=60\\Rightarrow x=30$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$30+20=3(30)-40=50$","En":"$30+20=3(30)-40=50$"}},"TrackIds":[8],"CategoryId":8,"PrimarySkillId":38,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"استعمل تساوي الزاويتين المتقابلتين.","En":"Use equality of vertical angles."},{"Ar":"ساو التعبيرين ثم اجمع حدود المجهول في طرف.","En":"Set the expressions equal, then collect variable terms."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"الزاويتان المتقابلتان بالرأس متساويتان.","En":"Vertically opposite angles are equal."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الزاويتان المتقابلتان بالرأس متساويتان.","En":"Vertical angles have equal measures."},{"Ar":"ننقل الحدود: 20+40=3x−x.","En":"Rearrange: 20+40=3x−x."},{"Ar":"نقسم 60 على 2 فنحصل على x=30.","En":"Divide 60 by two to find x=30."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$30$","En":"$30$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تجعل مجموع الزاويتين المتقابلتين 180؛ هذا للمجاورتين على مستقيم.","En":"Do not set vertical angles to sum to 180; that is for adjacent angles forming a straight line."},"FormulaLatex":"x+20=3x-40","Substitution":{"Ar":"$2x=60\\Rightarrow x=30$","En":"$2x=60\\Rightarrow x=30$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$30+20=3(30)-40=50$","En":"$30+20=3(30)-40=50$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"عند x=20 القياسان 40 و20 غير متساويين.","En":"At x=20 the measures are 40 and 20, unequal."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"عند x=40 القياسان 60 و80.","En":"At x=40 the measures are 60 and 80."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"عند x=60 القياسان 80 و140.","En":"At x=60 the measures are 80 and 140."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$الزاويتان المتقابلتان بالرأس متساويتان.

$x+20=3x-40$

1. الزاويتان المتقابلتان بالرأس متساويتان.

2. ننقل الحدود: 20+40=3x−x.

3. نقسم 60 على 2 فنحصل على x=30.

$2x=60\Rightarrow x=30$

$30$ بلا وحدة قياس

$30+20=3(30)-40=50$

لا تجعل مجموع الزاويتين المتقابلتين 180؛ هذا للمجاورتين على مستقيم.$mw$,$mw$Vertically opposite angles are equal.

$x+20=3x-40$

1. Vertical angles have equal measures.

2. Rearrange: 20+40=3x−x.

3. Divide 60 by two to find x=30.

$2x=60\Rightarrow x=30$

$30$ Dimensionless

$30+20=3(30)-40=50$

Do not set vertical angles to sum to 180; that is for adjacent angles forming a straight line.$mw$),
(717,702,$mw$F3DEA7A00DBC76E28298A4F7FE48AC82F2840421DC609680C5597A920010D4D3$mw$,$mw$7718a99a73a79f93d1d170970fdc297c$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":702,"StageId":2,"CategoryId":8,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"حساب قياس زاوية بعد حل متغير التساوي","TitleEn":"Find an angle measure after solving for the variable","QuestionTextAr":"زاويتان متقابلتان بالرأس قياساهما (2x + 5)° و(x + 35)°. ما قياس **إحداهما**؟","QuestionTextEn":"Two vertically opposite angles measure (2x + 5)° and (x + 35)°. What is the measure of either angle?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المبدأ المستخدم: الزوايا المتقابلة بالرأس متساوية. نكتب 2س + 5 = س + 35؛ بطرح س و5 نحصل على س = 30. لكن السؤال يطلب قياس الزاوية لا قيمة س؛ بالتعويض: 2 × 30 + 5 = 65°. والزاوية المقابلة تساوي 30 + 35 = 65°.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Rule used: Vertically opposite angles are equal, so 2x + 5 = x + 35 and x = 30. The question asks for the angle, not x. Substitute: 2 × 30 + 5 = 65°. The opposite angle is also 30 + 35 = 65°.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2753,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"30","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2754,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"35","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2755,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2756,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"65","IsCorrect":true}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"الزاويتان متساويتان، والمطلوب قياسهما لا المجهول.","En":"The angles are equal; the requested quantity is their measure, not the variable."},{"Ar":"حل معادلة التساوي ثم عوّض في أحد التعبيرين.","En":"Solve the equality and substitute into either expression."}],"Title":{"Ar":"حساب قياس زاوية بعد حل متغير التساوي","En":"Find an angle measure after solving for the variable"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"LatexCode":"30","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"30 قيمة x لا قياس الزاوية.","En":"Thirty is x, not the angle measure."}},{"LatexCode":"35","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35 ثابت في التعبير الثاني وليس القياس.","En":"Thirty-five is a constant in the second expression, not the measure."}},{"LatexCode":"60","IsCorrect":false,"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"60 ناتج 2x دون إضافة 5.","En":"Sixty is 2x without adding five."}},{"LatexCode":"65","IsCorrect":true,"ErrorType":"","Reason":null}],"StageId":2,"Question":{"Ar":"زاويتان متقابلتان بالرأس قياساهما (2x + 5)° و(x + 35)°. ما قياس **إحداهما**؟","En":"Two vertically opposite angles measure (2x + 5)° and (x + 35)°. What is the measure of either angle?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نساوي قياسي الزاويتين المتقابلتين ثم نعوض لإيجاد القياس.","En":"Equate vertical-angle measures, then substitute to find the measure."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نساوي التعبيرين لأنهما لزاويتين متقابلتين بالرأس.","En":"Equate expressions because the angles are vertical."},{"Ar":"نطرح x و5 من الطرفين فنحصل على x=30.","En":"Subtract x and five from both sides to obtain x=30."},{"Ar":"نعوض في أحد التعبيرين: 2×30+5=65.","En":"Substitute into either expression: 2×30+5=65."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$65$","En":"$65$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"المطلوب قياس الزاوية لا قيمة المجهول.","En":"The angle measure, not x, is requested."},"FormulaLatex":"2x+5=x+35","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=30,\\quad 2x+5=65$","En":"$x=30,\\quad 2x+5=65$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$30+35=65$","En":"$30+35=65$"}},"TrackIds":[8],"CategoryId":8,"PrimarySkillId":38,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"الزاويتان متساويتان، والمطلوب قياسهما لا المجهول.","En":"The angles are equal; the requested quantity is their measure, not the variable."},{"Ar":"حل معادلة التساوي ثم عوّض في أحد التعبيرين.","En":"Solve the equality and substitute into either expression."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"نساوي قياسي الزاويتين المتقابلتين ثم نعوض لإيجاد القياس.","En":"Equate vertical-angle measures, then substitute to find the measure."},"Unit":{"Ar":"درجة","En":"Degrees"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نساوي التعبيرين لأنهما لزاويتين متقابلتين بالرأس.","En":"Equate expressions because the angles are vertical."},{"Ar":"نطرح x و5 من الطرفين فنحصل على x=30.","En":"Subtract x and five from both sides to obtain x=30."},{"Ar":"نعوض في أحد التعبيرين: 2×30+5=65.","En":"Substitute into either expression: 2×30+5=65."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$65$","En":"$65$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"المطلوب قياس الزاوية لا قيمة المجهول.","En":"The angle measure, not x, is requested."},"FormulaLatex":"2x+5=x+35","Substitution":{"Ar":"$x=30,\\quad 2x+5=65$","En":"$x=30,\\quad 2x+5=65$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$30+35=65$","En":"$30+35=65$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"30 قيمة x لا قياس الزاوية.","En":"Thirty is x, not the angle measure."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"35 ثابت في التعبير الثاني وليس القياس.","En":"Thirty-five is a constant in the second expression, not the measure."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"60 ناتج 2x دون إضافة 5.","En":"Sixty is 2x without adding five."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$نساوي قياسي الزاويتين المتقابلتين ثم نعوض لإيجاد القياس.

$2x+5=x+35$

1. نساوي التعبيرين لأنهما لزاويتين متقابلتين بالرأس.

2. نطرح x و5 من الطرفين فنحصل على x=30.

3. نعوض في أحد التعبيرين: 2×30+5=65.

$x=30,\quad 2x+5=65$

$65$ درجة

$30+35=65$

المطلوب قياس الزاوية لا قيمة المجهول.$mw$,$mw$Equate vertical-angle measures, then substitute to find the measure.

$2x+5=x+35$

1. Equate expressions because the angles are vertical.

2. Subtract x and five from both sides to obtain x=30.

3. Substitute into either expression: 2×30+5=65.

$x=30,\quad 2x+5=65$

$65$ Degrees

$30+35=65$

The angle measure, not x, is requested.$mw$),
